Though I understand your reasoning behind that statement, I disagree 
with you on that. Potions in monster inventories being destroyed in 
neither all good nor all bad.

As Janis said down-thread, it prevents the monsters from using the 
various potions of healing. Monsters will also drink potions of gain 
level if they have one, so destroying those is not that bad (e.g., most 
of the times, you don't want that mind flayer facing you to grow into a 
master mind flayer).

With Frostbrand, there is a chance of destroying potions only but with 
Firebrand, there is a chance of destroying potions as well as scrolls. 
And I am using a +7 Firebrand as my main melee weapon in my current 
Ranger game.
Trust me, it isn't that bad. Most of the times monsters have either a 
scroll of create monster or a scroll of teleportation that gets burnt 
and you won't miss those.

You have several ways of farming for potions/scroll/wands/rings if you 
have been really unfortunate in that aspect of the game.
I am doing throne farming in my current game as I have not seen several 
useful amulets, rings and wands. You also get a ton of potions and 
scrolls that way.


